# Published Google Sheet CSV URL.
# In Google Sheets: File → Share → Publish to web → (sheet) → CSV → copy the URL.
# Must be PUBLIC_-prefixed so Astro exposes it to the client (the URL is public anyway).
PUBLIC_STICKER_CSV_URL=

# The /submit upload page needs two Worker secrets (NOT .env vars) — set them with
# `wrangler secret put`:  SHEET_WEBHOOK_URL, SHEET_WEBHOOK_TOKEN. See README → Submissions.

# ── Street View (optional) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ONE Google Maps key powers the whole feature (Google Cloud project, billing
# enabled — usage is $0). It's a *runtime* secret (NOT a build var): /api/streetview
# uses it server-side for the free coverage check and also hands it to the client
# for the embed iframe. Restrict it to the Maps Embed API + Street View Static API
# + your HTTP referrers (stickers.siddharthbobba.com/*, localhost:8787/*).
# Locally it can live here; in prod: `wrangler secret put GOOGLE_STREETVIEW_KEY`.
# Leave blank to disable Street View — the map works without it.
GOOGLE_STREETVIEW_KEY=

# ── CARTO dark basemap key (optional) ──────────────────────────────────────
# CARTO watermarks "API KEY REQUIRED" across keyless basemaps.cartocdn.com
# tiles (they still return HTTP 200, so the watermark is the only symptom).
# A free CARTO account clears it. Like the Street View key this is a *runtime*
# secret, not a build var: /api/basemap hands it to the client, which appends
# it to each tile URL as ?key=. Request one at https://carto.com/basemaps/apikey
# (free, emailed back, no account needed; 5M tile requests/month, attribution
# must stay visible). Restrict it to your domain in the CARTO dashboard.
# In prod: `wrangler secret put CARTO_BASEMAP_KEY`.
# Leave blank to fall back to Esri's keyless dark canvas.
CARTO_BASEMAP_KEY=

# ── Admin moderation queue (/admin) ────────────────────────────────────────
# Shared password for the officer sign-in that gates the pending-submission
# queue. Runtime secret, checked in constant time by /api/admin/login; unset
# means every login is refused (the queue fails closed, never open).
# In prod: `wrangler secret put ADMIN_PASSWORD` — type it yourself, don't paste
# it into a file that could be committed.
ADMIN_PASSWORD=
